ons and Politics","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"E000246","district":11,"fullName":"Rep. Edwards, Chuck [R-NC-11]","party":"R","state":"NC"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-03","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Equal Representation Act</strong></p><p>This bill requires that the statement sent by the President to Congress after the decennial census indicating the number of persons in each state&nbsp;exclude&nbsp;noncitizens. (This&nbsp;statement is the basis for reapportionment of U.S. Representatives.)</p><p>The bill also requires&nbsp;any questionnaire used in the&nbsp;decennial census to include a checkbox or other similar option for respondents to indicate whether the respondent and each household member is (1) a U.S. citizen, (2) a U.S. national but not a citizen, (3) a non-U.S. national (<em>alien </em>under federal law) lawfully residing in the United States, or (4) a non-U.S. national unlawfully residing in the United States.</p><p>The Department of Commerce must make public the number of persons in each state, disaggregated by each of these four categories.</p>","updateDate":"2025-04-17T21:07:33Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Equal Representation Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:18:02Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:18:02Z"}
